Subject: [PATCH] pco: retain fine derivatives in unmodified single encodings

Applies to Mesa 26.2.1, commit
da14d65e4499e66468094be52bff9ea0915a695e (third_party/mesa-pco.lock).

FDSXF/FDSYF already use dsxf/dsyf with source modifiers, but their short
I_SNGL encodings mistakenly selected the coarse dsx/dsy operations. Preserve
the explicit fine mode independent of whether the source has modifiers.
This changes native compiler encoding, not CTS results or the ISS decoder.

diff --git a/src/imagination/pco/pco_map.py b/src/imagination/pco/pco_map.py
--- a/src/imagination/pco/pco_map.py
+++ b/src/imagination/pco/pco_map.py
@@ -1068,7 +1068,7 @@ encode_map(O_FDSXF,
          ('s0neg', (RM_NEG, SRC(0))),
          ('s0abs', (RM_ABS, SRC(0)))
       ]),
-      (I_SNGL, [('sngl_op', 'dsx')], [
+      (I_SNGL, [('sngl_op', 'dsxf')], [
          (RM_NEG, SRC(0), '== false'),
          (RM_ABS, SRC(0), '== false')
       ])
@@ -1104,7 +1104,7 @@ encode_map(O_FDSYF,
          ('s0neg', (RM_NEG, SRC(0))),
          ('s0abs', (RM_ABS, SRC(0)))
       ]),
-      (I_SNGL, [('sngl_op', 'dsy')], [
+      (I_SNGL, [('sngl_op', 'dsyf')], [
          (RM_NEG, SRC(0), '== false'),
          (RM_ABS, SRC(0), '== false')
       ])
